{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"f529e0ba704de883c96d689c","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2evidence-dist","claim:pm-7wzc6f","claim:pm-gh1383","claim:pm-gh1385","lineage:pm-2evidence-dist","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-2evidence-dist+pm-7wzc6f+pm-gh1383+pm-gh1385","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2evidence-dist","claim:pm-7wzc6f","claim:pm-gh1383","claim:pm-gh1385","lineage:pm-2evidence-dist","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"GitHub: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1386\n\nThe current installed `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.10.4 emits an unchanged retry for a conflicting get projection when the conflicting selector is the global `--output-include` flag. This reproduces with `--no-extensions`; no custom extension is involved.\n\n```bash\npm --no-extensions get pm-a1b2 --full --output-budget unbounded --output-include item,linked,claim_state\n```\n\nThe command exits 2 before item lookup with `Get projection options are mutually exclusive; remove the extra projection flag and retry.` The recovery is:\n\n```text\nsuggested_retry: pm --no-extensions get pm-a1b2 --full --output-budget unbounded --output-include \"item,linked,claim_state\"\nattempted_command: pm --no-extensions get pm-a1b2 --full --output-budget unbounded --output-include \"item,linked,claim_state\"\n```\n\nExecuting the emitted retry repeats the same failure. As a control, `get pm-a1b2 --full --fields title` repairs its retry by removing `--fields`, so the global projection selector appears to be missed by conflict repair.\n\nExpected: preserve scope and unrelated options while removing one conflicting projection selector, or omit an automatic retry when the choice is ambiguous. The emitted argv should not preserve the known-invalid conflict.\n\nDuplicate check: searched all open and closed issues for projection, mutually exclusive, suggested_retry, full/output-include, and output-include/recovery. Read closed #1364 and open #1360. #1364 addresses dropped tracker/JSON scope; this report concerns a current unchanged conflict retry after that scope fix. #1360 defines authority-preserving recovery rather than this concrete global-selector repair failure.\n\nAcceptance: execute recovery argv for full/output-include conflicts (global option before/after subcommand and attached values), assert the projection conflict is gone and tracker/JSON scope remains unchanged; preserve the working full/fields repair case."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1386"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1386: remove conflicting global output projection from get recovery retries"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Reported on installed 2026.10.4: get --full combined with global --output-include emits suggested_retry identical to the rejected invocation. Preserve tracker/JSON scope and unrelated options while removing one conflicting selector or withholding an ambiguous retry. Intake only; this combined delivery has not independently reproduced or implemented this newly arrived report."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","context-management","github-intake"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Execute emitted recovery argv for full/output-include conflicts with options before and after subcommand and attached values;Projection conflict is removed while tracker and JSON scope remain unchanged;Existing full/fields repair continues to work;Ambiguous corrections do not emit known-invalid retries"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-f05lsg"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Refusal recovery produces executable argv without repeating a known projection conflict."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Reporter shows unchanged attempted_command and suggested_retry and repeated exit 2; no independent implementation claim."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-7wzc6f","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-f05lsg","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1360","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1364","kind":"verifies","created_at":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-04T04:48:35.056Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"All-status duplicate check: searched the complete 2,869-item corpus for projection conflict, mutually exclusive selectors and output-include recovery, ran request-specific CLI search, and refreshed live open/in-progress